  "cause": {
    "proximate_text": "less than adequate incorporation, internalization, and anchoring of operating and in-house experiences as it pertains to the unique design vulnerabilities in the DBNPS DC distribution system; a similar issue occurred in 2010 when a component was installed onto the DC system but was not rated for the conditions present within the system, and those learnings were not anchored into design documents or specifications, resulting in EDG speed switches with components (an MOV rated 170 VDC) not rated for the maximum possible voltage seen on the ungrounded 125 VDC system",
    "cause_code": "TBD",
    "category": "provisional",
    "theme": "operating experience not incorporated into DC system design/component selection",
    "provisional": true
  },
